<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Shirley</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1694">1694</a>–<a href="/years/1771">1771</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Shirley was a British lawyer and governor of the Province of Massachusetts Bay from 1741 to 1749 and 1753 to 1756. He organised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a> expedition that captured the French fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisbourg">Louisbourg</a> in 1745 and briefly commanded British forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> in the French and Indian War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-shirley.jpg" alt="William Shirley" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Hudson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WilliamShirleyNPG.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
